<title>ISRAEL: Elbit Medical Imaging 3Q EPS $0.08.</title>
<headline>Elbit Medical Imaging 3Q EPS $0.08.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-12-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's Elbit Medical Imaging Ltd, a subsidiary of Elron Electronic Industries Ltd.</p>
<p>			     (in thousands of dollars except EPS)</p>
<p>			   Q3 96	Q3 95     9-MTH 96    9-MTH 95</p>
<p>Revenue		  128,503    129,731   370,447     385,602</p>
<p>Operating Profit	 3,163	2,433     6,474	 8,824</p>
<p>Net Profit		 1,685	1,260     4,962	 4,964</p>
<p>Earnings per Share	0.08	 0.06	0.23	  0.23</p>
<p>Elbit Medical Imaging, a maker of medical electronics equipment, reported its third-quarter and nine-month results for 1995 on a pro forma basis. The company is one of two spun off from Elbit Ltd and began trading as a separate company in November.</p>
<p>The company said the increase in third-quarter net profit from the year-earlier period was due to improved operating profitability at its Elbit Ultrasound unit. This was offset by lower earnings at Elscint Ltd whose products came under price pressure mainly in Europe.</p>
<p>Elbit Medical Imaging said it had not yet determined a dividend policy but would be paying its share of a dividend declared by its predecessor company's board, $0.0318 a share payable Janaury 20, 1997.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
